  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Geo Group obligated $859M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Geo Group won 108 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $8M, and obligations are up 8.6% year over year. Obligations have trended higher from FY21 through FY26: FY21 $647M, FY22 $609M, FY23 $604M, FY24 $642M, FY25 $791M, FY26 $859M. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer of Geo Group services, obligating $714M in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Justice with $145M. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest NAICS market for Geo Group at $552M, followed by Facilities Support Services at $181M, Other Justice, Public Order, and Safety Activities at $81M, and Correctional Institutions at $46M. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. This summary focuses on obligations and market concentration so contractors and contracting officers can see where Geo Group is most active and which agencies drive the bulk of current spending.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who is buying from Geo Group in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security obligated $714M from Geo Group in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $145M. These two agencies account for the majority of Geo Group obligations this fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services is Geo Group supplying to the federal government?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is Geo Group's largest market at $552M in FY2026 to date. Facilities Support Services follows at $181M, Other Justice, Public Order, and Safety Activities at $81M, and Correctional Institutions at $46M."
      }
    ]
  },
